## Video Introduction

《Probably the Most Un-Tool-Like Tool I've Used Recently》demonstrates how SayAll transforms a Bluetooth voice remote control into a new gateway for effortless expression, computer control, and AI collaboration. The product interface in the video reflects the demonstration version at that time.

  </a>
</p>

Video author: [Cola's Not-So-Sweet Out-of-Focus Diary](https://space.bilibili.com/327214328)

SayAll Wireless Microphone Windows Edition has completed Windows native device adaptation for Xiaomi Bluetooth remote control 2 (RC001) and 2 Pro (RC003), covering verified scenarios including device identification, connection, key mapping, and voice bridging. The project uses Rust, Tauri 2, and Vue 3, with separate maintenance and releases for Windows and macOS.

Reference source repository: [HD838A/remote-mic-app](https://github.com/HD838A/remote-mic-app) (macOS Edition). The Windows version maintains an independent platform implementation, only referencing its publicly available product behavior, protocol experience, and testing boundaries, without feeding back to the macOS codebase.

The current repository is in the new architecture development phase. The following has been established at this stage:

- Settings interface skeleton in the style of the original Mac version;
- Pure Rust core for ATVV, IMA/DVI ADPCM, and voice sessions;
- WinRT paired device scanning, standard GATT Model Number (2A24) model identification, connection/notification/release, and session pipeline from RC001/RC003 to PCM;
- User-selected WASAPI shared mode output endpoint, bounded PCM queue, and padding flush;
- User choices persisted with stable endpoint ID and name, restoring only endpoints with completely matching identity at startup;
- Remembers user-selected RC001 or RC003, with exponential backoff auto-reconnection between 2–30 seconds; actively releases sessions when Windows sleeps, rebuilds GATT/ATVV after resumption;
- Real-time status interface distinguishing connection, characteristic discovery, capability confirmation, ready, streaming reception, flushing, disconnection, and failure;
- Device path-limited Raw Input, batch SendInput, mapping persistence, and explicit shortcut key testing;
- Daily key presses, complete voice sessions, and voice duration statistics saved only locally, with display options for today, this week, all, and last 7 days;
- Dual-layer version gate for Windows 10 1809 (build 17763) installation and startup;
